<section class="saas-legal-page">
  <div class="saas-container saas-page-shell">
    <div class="saas-page-hero">
      <p class="saas-legal-kicker">Holiday Stickers</p>

      <h1>Christmas AI Sticker Maker</h1>

      <p>
        Make Christmas stickers with AI from a short prompt. Generate festive characters, cozy
        winter icons, and holiday reactions, then download PNG or WebP files. Try 3 generations
        with no sign up.
      </p>
      <a class="saas-button saas-button-primary" href="/#generator">
        Make a Christmas Sticker
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="saas-info-grid">
      <article class="saas-info-panel">
        <h2>Holiday characters</h2>

        <p>
          Describe one festive subject: a cocoa mug, gift box mascot, tree ornament character, or
          cozy winter portrait.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="saas-info-panel">
        <h2>Keep the prompt simple</h2>

        <p>
          Add a sticker job and a holiday mood. Too many decorations in one prompt usually make a
          weaker silhouette.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="saas-info-panel">
        <h2>Use it for chats and cards</h2>

        <p>
          Generated files are sticker-style images you can download for messages, cards, and
          social posts. This is an AI generator, not a printed sticker shop.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>How to make Christmas stickers with AI</h2>

      <ol>
        <li>Describe a Christmas subject such as a cozy tree, gift mascot, or festive portrait.</li>

        <li>Add holiday style words like clean border, snowy colors, or cute winter icon.</li>

        <li>Generate one sticker or a small set of holiday prompts.</li>

        <li>Download PNG or WebP files for chats, cards, and social posts.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>Christmas AI sticker prompt examples</h2>

      <div class="saas-prompt-list">
        <code>cute cocoa mug mascot sticker, cozy smile, snowflakes, clean white border</code>
        <code>gift box character waving, festive red and green, simple background</code>
        <code>sleepy polar bear with scarf, winter sticker, rounded outline</code>
        <code>christmas tree ornament with face, kawaii holiday sticker</code>
        <code>gingerbread cookie mascot, cheerful smile, icing details, clean white border</code>
        <code>snow globe character, cozy winter mood, rounded outline, simple background</code>
        <code>festive reindeer reaction sticker, surprised expression, bold holiday colors</code>
        <code>winter penguin holding a gift, cute scarf, crisp silhouette, sticker style</code>
        <code>holiday candle mascot, warm glow, friendly face, minimal festive background</code>
        <code>cozy snowman waving, knitted hat, soft blue and red palette, clean border</code>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>Christmas sticker ideas for chats and cards</h2>

      <p>
        Start with one holiday subject and one readable emotion. A cocoa mug, gift box, ornament,
        gingerbread cookie, snow globe, reindeer, or winter animal gives the sticker a clear shape.
        Add a simple action such as waving, smiling, cheering, sleeping, or giving a gift when you
        want the result to work as a reaction in a conversation.
      </p>

      <p>
        For greeting cards and social posts, describe the mood and palette after the subject. Cozy
        winter colors, snowy blue, festive red and green, warm candlelight, or soft pastel holiday
        colors can guide the direction. Keep the scene simple so the subject remains recognizable
        when the image is viewed at a small size.
      </p>

      <p>
        To make a matching Christmas sticker set, repeat the same style words in every prompt and
        change only the subject or emotion. Batch mode can help you create several related prompts,
        but each prompt still works best when it focuses on one main holiday idea.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>Holiday sticker files on mobile</h2>

      <p>
        You can create a Christmas sticker from a phone or desktop browser. Text prompts are useful
        when you want a mascot, object, or fictional holiday character. Portrait mode is useful for
        a festive avatar or reaction based on a clear photo. In either case, review the output at
        the size where people will actually see it before choosing a favorite.
      </p>

      <p>
        PNG is a practical download for editing and broad compatibility. WebP is usually smaller
        for websites, previews, and chats. Platform upload tools may add their own requirements for
        dimensions, transparency, animation, and file size, so check the destination platform before
        building a complete pack.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>AI Christmas stickers, not printed packs</h2>

      <p>
        This Christmas AI sticker maker is for generating new holiday artwork. If you want to buy
        physical sticker packs, a print shop is a better fit. If you want to create a custom
        festive sticker from a prompt, start on the generator.
      </p>

      <div class="saas-related-links">
        <.link navigate={~p"/ai-sticker-generator"}>AI Sticker Generator</.link>
        <.link navigate={~p"/reaction-sticker-maker"}>Reaction Sticker Maker</.link>
        <.link navigate={~p"/kawaii-sticker-maker"}>Kawaii Sticker Maker</.link>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="saas-faq">
      <details open>
        <summary>Can I make Christmas stickers with AI?</summary>

        <p>
          Yes. Write a holiday prompt or upload a festive portrait and generate a sticker-style
          image.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Do I need to sign up?</summary>

        <p>No. Guests can try 3 Christmas sticker generations without an account.</p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>What Christmas sticker ideas work well?</summary>

        <p>
          Keep one subject: a cocoa mug, tree ornament character, gift box mascot, or cozy winter
          portrait.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>What should I include in a Christmas sticker prompt?</summary>

        <p>
          Name one holiday subject, then add an emotion, action, palette, and simple sticker style.
          For example, try a cheerful gingerbread cookie waving with a clean white border.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Can I make a matching Christmas sticker set?</summary>

        <p>
          Yes. Repeat the same border, palette, and style words while changing the subject or
          emotion. Batch mode supports one Christmas prompt per line for a small set.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Can I use a portrait for a Christmas sticker?</summary>

        <p>
          Yes. Upload a clear portrait and add a festive style prompt for a holiday avatar or
          reaction. No account is required for the 3 free guest generations.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Which download format should I use?</summary>

        <p>
          PNG is convenient for editing and compatibility. WebP is usually smaller for websites,
          previews, and chats.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
